# Volatile Fault: ruling 2023-11-10 - the search and the Treasure do not depend on the land being destroyed. In response Bot2
# animates Creeping Tar Pit and gives it indestructible (Revitalizing Repast); the target is still legal, so Bot2 may still
# search (Forest) and Bot1 still creates a Treasure. Also shows {T}: Add {C} (the Fault taps for it before it is spent).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Island
Volatile Fault
Island x16
Plains

[Bot2 Deck]
Creeping Tar Pit
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Revitalizing Repast
Island x14
Island
Forest

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Creeping Tar Pit.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Volatile Fault.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Volatile Fault.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot2.Battlefield.Creeping Tar Pit)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Creeping Tar Pit.Activate(Ability: Until end of turn)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Creeping Tar Pit.Activate(Ability: {T}: Add {U} or {B}; Color: Black)
Bot2.Hand.Revitalizing Repast.Cast(Creeping Tar Pit)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Search(Forest)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Volatile Fault
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Treasure Token
Bot2.Graveyard = Revitalizing Repast
Bot2.Battlefield.Creeping Tar Pit.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = false
